# The DAST run's client (docs/plan/PLAN.md F6e.1): a service client (client credentials) for the scanners, defined only
# here. .github/workflows/dast.yml loads this file into the throwaway host's environment and adds the client's secret,
# generated for that run (openssl rand) and never written to a file (Y-35). No committed appsettings file holds this
# client, so no other host seeds it (DastClientTests).
#
# Lines are environment variables, sourced by bash (no spaces or quotes in a value); "__" is ":" to the configuration
# (Identity:Clients:100:ClientId). The index is past the committed files' clients: configuration merges arrays by index,
# so a lower one would write over the Development file's `scalar` client instead of adding this one.
#
# Permissions: the read permission of every endpoint in the OpenAPI document that asks for one (their GETs), so the
# scanners reach the handlers behind the permission check. No write permission (the scan would change data through
# them, and the anonymous endpoints already take writes), and not payments:read-all, which only widens what a read
# returns.
Identity__Clients__100__ClientId=dast
Identity__Clients__100__DisplayName=DAST-scanner
Identity__Clients__100__Permissions__0=catalog:products:read
Identity__Clients__100__Permissions__1=payments:read
Identity__Clients__100__Permissions__2=identity:users:read
Identity__Clients__100__Permissions__3=identity:roles:read
